codex
The patch leaves a state-derived path in the generated manifest outside the citation verification machinery, so a broken publish-gate pin can pass verification. This contradicts the tool's stated contract and can produce misleading commission briefs.

Review comment:

- [P2] Verify the state-derived pinned path — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/dh2-fix/scripts/commission-manifest.sh:423-423
  When `acceptance.publish_gate.pre_sign.pinned_to` is mistyped or points to a renamed file, the manifest still prints that path but `--verify` reports 0 dead citations because this line emits it as raw text instead of registering it with `m.cite(...)`. That violates the manifest's CHECK 1 guarantee that every cited path exists, and can brief an orchestrator with a dead pin path while CI stays green.
